  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-236888\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>A polygon is <strong>simple</strong> if its boundary does not intersect itself. Otherwise, the polygon is called <strong>complex</strong>.</p>\n<p>Among the given polygons, only polygon II has intersecting sides. </p>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"</p>\n<div class=\"studentAnswerHeader\">Your Answer:</div><div class=\"studentAnswer\">II and III only</div></div>",
